    "_error_map_note": "Story 26.2 (dossier section 7): keys are '<http_status>:<ENUM_VALUE_NAME>' -- Google REST payloads carry enum NAMES inside error.details[].errors[].errorCode, not numbers. The connector extracts the enum itself (_extract_error_enum) because the generic core extractor only reads error.code (the numeric HTTP echo). 429/RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED is NOT in this map: it stays on the core.quota.RateLimitError breaker path, honoring QuotaErrorDetails.retry_delay. 400:UNSUPPORTED_VERSION additionally raises the loud version-drift alert (google_ads_unsupported_version_drift). Any 400 QueryError on a cataloged field is the catalog drift signal (pull_invalid_request_drift).",
    "refetch": {
        "nightly_days": 14,
        "weekly_days": 35,
        "monthly_days": 90,
        "_note": "Dossier section 6: interaction-date conversion metrics are restated for up to the account's click-through conversion window (1-90 days, default 30). nightly_days=14 matches the Airbyte conversion_window_days default; weekly deep re-pull 35d; monthly re-pull 90d covers the maximum window. Date segments are capped at a 37-month lookback (backfill bound)."
    },
