    "account_topology": {
        "_comment": "Story 26.2 (pattern 25.5): Google Ads hierarchy = manager (MCC, nested up to 6 levels) -> client account. The reporting entity (selection_level) is the CLIENT ACCOUNT -- managers hold no metrics (REQUESTED_METRICS_FOR_MANAGER). discover_accounts = CustomerService.listAccessibleCustomers + customer_client GAQL expansion per seed (flattened labeled tree, manager flag, ENABLED filter). Child accounts reached through a manager carry the composite opaque id '<client_cid>@<login_cid>' so the pull resolves login-customer-id without re-discovery. Core owns selection/access-check/trial/backfill; GOOGLE_ADS_*_ID env vars are FORBIDDEN (doctrine).",
        "levels": [
            {
                "id": "manager",
                "label": "Manager account (MCC)"
            },
            {
                "id": "client_account",
                "label": "Client account"
            }
        ],
        "selection_level": "client_account",
        "discovery": {
            "callable": "discover_accounts"
        }
    }
